"We are given the following information:\n\n- Wendi feeds her chickens **three times a day**.\n- Each feeding is a **certain number of cups**.\n- The **total feed per day** is the **sum of the three meals**.\n- The **flock size is 20 chickens**.\n- The **feed per chicken** is **3 cups per meal** (since each chicken gets 3 cups in total per day, split into 3 meals).\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Total feed per chicken per day\n\nEach chicken gets 3 cups of feed per day, split into 3 meals.  \nSo, **each chicken gets 1 cup per meal**.\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Total feed per day for 20 chickens\n\nEach chicken gets 1 cup per meal, and there are 3 meals per day.\n\n$$\n\\text{Total feed per day} = 20 \\text{ chickens} \\times 3 \\text{ cups/day} = 60 \\text{ cups/day}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Feed given in the first two meals\n\n- Morning: 15 cups  \n- Afternoon: 25 cups  \n$$\n\\text{Total in first two meals} = 15 + 25 = 40 \\text{ cups}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 4: Feed needed for the final meal\n\n$$\n\\text{Final meal feed} = \\text{Total feed per day} - \\text{Feed in first two meals}\n$$\n$$\n\\text{Final meal feed} = 60 - 40 = 20 \\text{ cups}\n$$\n\n---\n\n**Answer: 20**"
