"We are given the following information:\n\n- Toulouse has **twice as many sheep as Charleston**.\n- Charleston has **4 times as many sheep as Seattle**.\n- **Seattle has 20 sheep**.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Find the number of sheep in **Charleston**\n\nCharleston has 4 times as many sheep as Seattle:\n\n$$\n\\text{Charleston} = 4 \\times \\text{Seattle} = 4 \\times 20 = 80\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Find the number of sheep in **Toulouse**\n\nToulouse has twice as many sheep as Charleston:\n\n$$\n\\text{Toulouse} = 2 \\times \\text{Charleston} = 2 \\times 80 = 160\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Add the number of sheep in all three cities\n\n$$\n\\text{Total} = \\text{Toulouse} + \\text{Charleston} + \\text{Seattle} = 160 + 80 + 20 = 260\n$$\n\n---\n\n**Answer: 260**"
