"We are given:\n\n- The candle melts by **2 centimeters every hour**.\n- The candle burns from **1:00 PM to 5:00 PM**.\n\n### Step 1: Find the total time the candle burns.\n\nFrom 1:00 PM to 5:00 PM is:\n\n$$\n5:00 - 1:00 = 4 \\text{ hours}\n$$\n\n### Step 2: Calculate the total melting.\n\nThe candle melts **2 cm per hour**, so over 4 hours:\n\n$$\n2 \\, \\text{cm/hour} \\times 4 \\, \\text{hours} = 8 \\, \\text{cm}\n$$\n\n### Final Answer:\n\nThe candle will be **8 centimeters shorter** after burning from 1:00 PM to 5:00 PM.\n\n**Answer: 8**"
