"We are given the following information:\n\n- The **bridge can carry no more than 5000 pounds**.\n- The **truck and driver together weigh 3755 pounds**.\n- Each **box weighs 15 pounds**.\n- We need to find the **maximum number of boxes** that can be loaded **without exceeding the bridge's weight limit**.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Determine the maximum total weight the bridge can carry\n\nThe bridge can carry **no more than 5000 pounds**.\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Determine how much weight can be added to the truck\n\nThe **truck and driver together weigh 3755 pounds**, so the **maximum additional weight** the truck can carry is:\n\n$$\n5000 - 3755 = 1245 \\text{ pounds}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Determine how many boxes can be loaded\n\nEach box weighs **15 pounds**, so the **maximum number of boxes** is:\n\n$$\n\\left\\lfloor \\frac{1245}{15} \\right\\rfloor = \\left\\lfloor 83 \\right\\rfloor = 83\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Final Answer:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{83}\n$$\n\n**Answer: 83**"
