"We are given the following information:\n\n- Rani has **10 more crabs** than Monic.\n- Monic has **4 fewer crabs** than Bo.\n- Bo has **40 crabs**.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Find how many crabs Monic has.\n\nMonic has 4 fewer crabs than Bo, and Bo has 40 crabs.\n\n$$\n\\text{Monic's crabs} = 40 - 4 = 36\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Find how many crabs Rani has.\n\nRani has 10 more crabs than Monic.\n\n$$\n\\text{Rani's crabs} = 36 + 10 = 46\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Add the number of crabs for all three.\n\n$$\n\\text{Total crabs} = \\text{Bo's crabs} + \\text{Monic's crabs} + \\text{Rani's crabs}\n$$\n$$\n= 40 + 36 + 46 = 122\n$$\n\n---\n\n**Answer: 122**"
