"Step 1: Find the total number of pails Baldur gets in a day.  \nHe gets 5 pails in the morning and 6 pails in the afternoon:  \n$$\n5 + 6 = 11 \\text{ pails}\n$$\n\nStep 2: Each pail contains 5 liters of water.  \nSo, the total amount of water he gets in a day is:  \n$$\n11 \\times 5 = 55 \\text{ liters}\n$$\n\nAnswer: 55"
"Let's break this down step by step.\n\n---\n\n### **Step 1: Understand the components of the award**\n\n- **One-time monetary reward**: $5000\n- **5% raise in salary**: This is a **one-time raise** applied to his **weekly salary**.\n- **Weekly salary**: $2000 per week\n- **Award received on the first day of the year**, so the raise is applied **immediately**.\n\n---\n\n### **Step 2: Calculate the raise in salary**\n\nA 5% raise on $2000:\n\n$$\n\\text{Raise} = 2000 \\times 0.05 = 100\n$$\n\nSo, his **new weekly salary** is:\n\n$$\n2000 + 100 = 2100\n$$\n\n---\n\n### **Step 3: Calculate total earnings from the regular salary**\n\nHe works **52 weeks** in a year, and his **new weekly salary** is $2100.\n\n$$\n\\text{Regular earnings} = 2100 \\times 52 = 109,200\n$$\n\n---\n\n### **Step 4: Add the one-time reward**\n\n$$\n\\text{Total earnings} = 109,200 + 5000 = 114,200\n$$\n\n---\n\n### **Final Answer:**\n\n$$\n\\boxed{114200}\n$$\n\n**Answer: 114200**"
"We are given the following information:\n\n- Josie has a **10-acre** farm.\n- Each **acre** produces **5 tons** of grapes per year.\n- Each **ton** of grapes makes **2 barrels** of wine.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Calculate total grape production per year\n\n$$\n\\text{Total grapes} = 10 \\text{ acres} \\times 5 \\text{ tons/acre} = 50 \\text{ tons}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Calculate total wine production per year\n\n$$\n\\text{Total wine} = 50 \\text{ tons} \\times 2 \\text{ barrels/ton} = 100 \\text{ barrels}\n$$\n\n---\n\n**Answer: 100**"
"Let's break this down step by step and calculate the total number of cheese slices Carl used during the week.\n\n---\n\n### **Step 1: Cheese used in sandwiches (lunch)**\n\n- Carl ate a **sandwich every day** for lunch.\n- He used **2 slices of cheese per sandwich**.\n- There are **7 days in a week**.\n\nSo, cheese used in sandwiches:\n$$\n7 \\text{ days} \\times 2 \\text{ slices/day} = 14 \\text{ slices}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### **Step 2: Cheese used in omelets (breakfast)**\n\n- Carl had **3 days** of **cheese and egg omelets** for breakfast.\n- Each omelet used **1 more slice of cheese** than a sandwich.\n- A sandwich uses **2 slices**, so an omelet uses:\n$$\n2 + 1 = 3 \\text{ slices per omelet}\n$$\n\nSo, cheese used in omelets:\n$$\n3 \\text{ days} \\times 3 \\text{ slices/day} = 9 \\text{ slices}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### **Step 3: Cheese used in macaroni and cheese dish**\n\n- Carl made **1 big dish of macaroni and cheese**.\n- It used **8 slices of cheese**.\n\n---\n\n### **Step 4: Total cheese used**\n\nNow, add up all the cheese used:\n\n- Sandwiches: 14 slices  \n- Omelets: 9 slices  \n- Macaroni and cheese: 8 slices  \n\n$$\n14 + 9 + 8 = 31 \\text{ slices}\n$$\n\n---\n\n**Answer: 31**"
